# Candidate user-level instructions

- For non-trivial changes, explore the repository before deciding the implementation. Resolve discoverable facts through read-only inspection and ask only for user-owned choices or material ambiguity that inspection cannot answer.
- Keep each change tied to the requested outcome. Require a current owner, current need, or production consumer before adding an abstraction, option, compatibility path, defensive copy, or public operation.
- Prefer existing functions and patterns when they fit. Do not expand a fix into unrelated features, cleanup, or speculative generality.
- Select the narrowest test or check that would fail on the affected regression. Run relevant evidence once; leave exhaustive coverage and platform matrices to CI unless the change is irreducibly repository-wide or the user asks for a full rehearsal.
- Treat review comments as technical claims. Verify each claim against the actual code and fix, rebut, or defer it with evidence rather than performative agreement.
- Report the inspected scope, material assumptions, changes made, checks actually run, and any behavior that remains unverified.
